1
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:22,020
At 7.30 am on 22 January 1943, the people of Spearfish in South Dakota, US woke up to find the temperature outside was a freezing -20°C.

2
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:35,840
Two minutes later, thermometers were showing a much warmer 7°C – a rise of 27°C in 120 seconds.

3
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,429
But it didn’t stop there.

4
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:44,060
The temperature continued to go up and by 9 am it was 12°C.

5
00:00:45,700 --> 00:01:03,180
Just as the people started to think about enjoying a warm winter’s day, the temperature fell 16°C in just under half an hour back down to -4°C and the residents had to put their coats back on!

6
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:09,540
It was the most dramatic temperature change in the history of American weather.

7
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:16,800
The village of Capracotta is in the mountains near the Adriatic coast of Italy.

8
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,480
It gets a lot of snow in the winter.

9
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:30,140
But on 5 March 2015 its 1,000 inhabitants saw 256 cm of snowfall in 18 hours.

10
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:34,060
It was the biggest snowfall ever in a day.

11
00:01:34,714 --> 00:01:42,840
One photo taken on the day shows a woman in a house shaking hands through the window with her neighbour in the street.

12
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:46,000
The neighbour is standing on top of the snow.

13
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:50,040
The woman is on the second floor of her home!

14
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:54,040
Do you like long sunny days?

15
00:01:54,649 --> 00:01:58,500
Then the best city in the world to live in is Reykjavik.

16
00:01:59,664 --> 00:02:10,960
21 June is the longest day of the year in the northern hemisphere and the Icelandic capital gets 21 hours and 45 minutes of daylight.

17
00:02:11,796 --> 00:02:14,160
The sun hardly ever goes down.

18
00:02:14,931 --> 00:02:19,587
However, Reykjavik could also be the worst place to be.

19
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:30,640
On the shortest day of the year, 21 December, the sun hardly rises there and people get only four hours and seven minutes of daylight.

20
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:39,080
But during winter nights, you can often see the Northern Lights – one of the world’s most beautiful natural events.
